<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orhan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Orhan was the second ruler of the Ottoman state, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osman-i">Osman I</a>. He captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bursa">Bursa</a> in 1326 and made it the dynasty's first proper capital. His reign marked the transition of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> from a raiding frontier confederation into a territorial state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orhan.jpg" alt="Orhan" width="251" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Metehanzade_orhangazi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
